    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "tbl_0039",
      "reading_order": 507,
      "section": "The buttons and what they do",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 35.47587244290107,
        "t": 470.6774744986427,
        "r": 558.5638469891201,
        "b": 236.6414923890983
      },
      "markdown": "| Button Meaning   | Function                                                                                                                                     |\n|------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Keyboard screen  | The keyboard screen is used to enter an authorised password to enter data for programmes and may restrict operator access to some functions. |\n| Clear screen     | Select the 'clear screen' key to delete text from the keyboard screen.                                                                       |\n| Keyboard         | Type in text using the keyboard.                                                                                                             |\n| Keyboard scroll  | Select the 'numbers' key to switch numbers & special characters keyboard. Press the 'letters' key to return to the letters keyboard.         |\n| Keyboard scroll  | Select the up arrow to scroll the keyboard screen for lowercase.                                                                             |\n| Enter / OK       | Select the green check mark to confirm settings and continue.                                                                                |\n| Previous screen  | Select the 'backspace' key to return to a previous screen.                                                                                   |",
      "rows": 8,
      "cols": 2,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_502",
